{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the degree measure of the angle at each vertex in the star-polygon formed by drawing a chord from each number to the fifth number counted clockwise from that number on a clock face. Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1. **Identify the vertices and the angle subtended at the center:**\n   - The vertices of the star-polygon are the numbers on the clock face: 12, 5, 10, 3, 8, 1, 6, 11, 4, 9, 2, 7.\n   - The angle subtended at the center by each side of the star-polygon is the angle between two radii that connect the center of the clock to two consecutive vertices of the star-polygon.\n   - Since the clock is a circle divided into 12 equal parts, the angle subtended at the center by each hour mark is \\(360^\\circ / 12 = 30^\\circ\\).\n   - The angle subtended at the center by the arc between two consecutive vertices of the star-polygon is \\(5 \\times 30^\\circ = 150^\\circ\\) (since we are skipping 4 numbers between each vertex).\n\n","prefix_end":973,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,8381,6629,315,279,9210,518,1817,11936,304,279,6774,2268,19582,14122,553,13330,264,43221,504,1817,1372,311,279,17702,1372,29994,65670,504,429,1372,389,264,8866,3579,13,6771,594,1438,432,1495,3019,553,3019,382,16,13,3070,28301,1437,279,17228,323,279,9210,41029,2883,518,279,4126,25,1019,256,481,576,17228,315,279,6774,2268,19582,525,279,5109,389,279,8866,3579,25,220,16,17,11,220,20,11,220,16,15,11,220,18,11,220,23,11,220,16,11,220,21,11,220,16,16,11,220,19,11,220,24,11,220,17,11,220,22,624,256,481,576,9210,41029,2883,518,279,4126,553,1817,3108,315,279,6774,2268,19582,374,279,9210,1948,1378,11900,72,429,4564,279,4126,315,279,8866,311,1378,23921,17228,315,279,6774,2268,19582,624,256,481,8704,279,8866,374,264,12671,17779,1119,220,16,17,6144,5479,11,279